# The Underground Network, C2-S12 Wraith Recognition, B03 Data Wraith,
# C2-S13 the Data Wraith choice. Source: Production Master 2.1, lines 2409–2499.
# Scene: scenes/chapter2/underground_network.tscn.
# Source fix: the Wraith no longer says "MARA" (Oakhaven's baker); the name it
# reaches for is a missing worker's, which the shift records can confirm.
# Chapters 4, 5 and 10 read ch2_data_wraith_restored / _destroyed / _absorbed.
# rhythm: clipped destroy
# (The destroy exchange is deliberately bare. Nobody wants to say more.)

~ entry
Kaelen (Internal): The stone stops after the first stairs. Underneath, it's conduits. Cable runs. Junction boxes older than the city.
Seraphina: You know this place. Don't tell me you don't.
Kaelen: Not this place. The way it's built. I've seen wiring like this before.
Seraphina: I don't love how you said that.
Elara: You get used to it. I didn't, but you might.
[if ch2_shift_sealed] Kaelen (Internal): A night's made it worse. The lights are wrong all the way down.
[if ch2_shift_rescue_now] Kaelen (Internal): We're going in fast and half-ready. Seraphina hasn't stopped counting since the stairs.

# Workers caught in pockets of repeating time.
~ workers
Worker: Shift starts at six. Shift starts at six. Is it six yet?
Seraphina: It's well past six. You're coming with me.
Worker: I clocked out. I remember clocking out. I've never once clocked out of this shift.

# The Wraith speaks through the lights before it shows itself.
~ wraith_lights
do lights_flicker
Data Wraith: IDENTIFY.
Data Wraith: HANNA.
Data Wraith: NO.
Data Wraith: SESSION RESTORE.
Data Wraith: PLEASE DON'T.
Data Wraith: RESTORE.

# C2-S12 — Kaelen sees what it is.
~ recognition
do data_vision_wraith
Kaelen: It isn't one ghost. It isn't lots of separate people, either. Something tried to restore them all at once, and they ran together.
Seraphina: Are they in pain? Any of them?
Kaelen: I think so. I think all of them are.
Data Wraith: YES.
Data Wraith: NO.
Data Wraith: DEFINE.
Elara: That sounded like you.
Kaelen: I know. It sounded exactly like me.
do wraith_hostile

# ── B03 barks ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
~ bark_restore
Data Wraith: RESTORE.

~ bark_identify
Data Wraith: IDENTIFY.

~ bark_please
Data Wraith: PLEASE.

# C2-S13 — no fourth, obviously perfect option.
~ choice
set ch2_data_wraith_defeated
do wraith_unstable
? Kaelen (Internal): It's still running. It's still them.
- Restore it. Try to pull the people apart. (Some may not come back whole.) => restore
- Destroy it. End the process. (Anyone still recoverable is lost.) => destroy
- Absorb it. Hold them in my Root layer until there's a better answer. (Corruption. Identity bleed.) => absorb

~ restore
set ch2_data_wraith_restored
do root_edit wraith_separate
Kaelen (Internal): Records. Shift lists. Anything with a name on it.
do wraith_split
Iven: My name's Iven.
Kaelen: Iven. Got it. Iven.
Iven: Don't lose it. I nearly did.
do kaelen_writes_name
Kaelen (Internal): I write it down. I write it down twice.

~ destroy
set ch2_data_wraith_destroyed
Seraphina: Are you sure?
Kaelen: No.
Seraphina: That isn't what I asked.
Kaelen: It's still the answer.
do wraith_ends
# The lights go out, one by one, all the way down the tunnel.

~ absorb
set ch2_data_wraith_absorbed
do absorb_wraith
Elara: Tell me this is safe. Just say it, even if you're guessing.
Kaelen: It isn't. It really isn't.
Elara: Then thank you for not lying to me.
# The fragments go into him. His corruption climbs. Later, the voices come back as single words.

# The routing junction in the puzzle chamber.
~ routing
Kaelen (Internal): A routing junction. If I swing this thread over... There. The way down's open.
